<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Initial evaluation and safety: blood count, iron studies and metabolic panel; Glasgow-Blatchford score; stop ibuprofen and all NSAIDs and use acetaminophen; urgent upper endoscopy within three days; no acid-suppressing medicine or antibiotic before the biopsies unless bleeding recurs; call 119 or go to the emergency department at once for black or bloody stools, vomiting blood or coffee-ground material, fainting, or severe pain. Guideline: ACG Clinical Guideline: Treatment of Helicobacter pylori Infection (2024); Evidence-based clinical practice guidelines for peptic ulcer disease 2026 (2026); ACG Clinical Guideline: Upper Gastrointestinal and Ulcer Bleeding (2021) [S]</item><item>Urgent gastroenterology consultation for upper endoscopy with biopsy within three days, to find the cause of the bleeding, exclude gastric cancer, test for Helicobacter pylori, and advise on treatment. Guideline: Evidence-based clinical practice guidelines for peptic ulcer disease 2026 (2026); ACG Clinical Guideline: Upper Gastrointestinal and Ulcer Bleeding (2021) [S]</item><item>Iron-deficiency anemia: oral iron once the source is found at endoscopy; blood count about four weeks after starting iron and then every three months for a year; continue iron about three months after the hemoglobin is normal and until ferritin is replete; colonoscopy if the anemia does not correct once the ulcer has healed. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, anemia monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Stress and sleep: PHQ-9 and GAD-7 at intake and at the end of the episode; regular meals, a fixed bedtime, and writing hours that leave the evening free; counselling if scores rise. Guideline: Depression and Suicide Risk in Adults: Screening (2023) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
